{"_id":"68a7360d8ec3d8323af123da","nodeId":"LAdKDJ4LcMaDWqslMvE8X","roadmapSlug":"backend","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:06:53.149Z","description":"# CAP Theorem\n\nCAP Theorem states distributed systems can only guarantee two of three properties: Consistency (same data across nodes), Availability (system responds to requests), and Partition tolerance (operates despite network failures). Guides distributed system design decisions and database selection.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"What is CAP Theorem?","url":"https://www.bmc.com/blogs/cap-theorem/","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4592"},{"type":"article","title":"An Illustrated Proof of the CAP Theorem","url":"https://mwhittaker.github.io/blog/an_illustrated_proof_of_the_cap_theorem/","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4593"},{"type":"article","title":"CAP Theorem and its applications in NoSQL Databases","url":"https://www.ibm.com/uk-en/cloud/learn/cap-theorem","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4594"},{"type":"video","title":"What is CAP Theorem?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_RbsFXWRZ10","_id":"6a7588bab0650226a5eb4595"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T07:26:50.654Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d04169a5","title":"roadmap.sh - Master SQL","partner":"roadmap.sh","type":"course","url":"https://roadmap.sh/courses/sql"},{"_id":"6a5e04ddfb5fcb94d04169cc","title":"Scrimba - Backend Developer Career Path","partner":"Scrimba","type":"course","url":"http://scrimba.com/the-backend-developer-path-c0tbi0l98f?via=roadmap"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/backend/content/LAdKDJ4LcMaDWqslMvE8X.md"}
